time and effort, and *you* don't seem willing to spend it. No offence
intended.

> and The really awful way the oracle talks. (you can be obtuse without
> being awkward.)

I think this is intended indeed. She intentionally speaks oldfashioned,
and intentionally cryptic. The first only enhances the second.

> This Yani is only going to address classes.

Good, since we seem to agree that more variation is necessary and
possible here.

> Before i start however, here i the guidelines i want to keep in mind.
